---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import '../../styles/lab.css';
---
<SiteLayout title="About — Worldeology Lab" description="Worldeology Lab is a distributed research lab building the foundations of Cognitive AI." headerTone="paper" active="about" image="/og.png">
  <main id="main" class="lab-site lab-page about-page">
    <header class="lab-page-hero about-page-hero">
      <p class="lab-index">Worldeology Lab / About</p>
      <h1>About</h1>
      <p>An independent research lab building the foundations of Cognitive AI.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="lab-page-section about-part" aria-labelledby="lab-title">
      <header><p class="lab-index">01</p><h2 id="lab-title">Who we are.</h2></header>
      <div class="lab-prose">
        <p>Worldeology Lab is a distributed, researcher-led lab working across machine learning, social cognition, model alignment, and world modeling.</p>
        <p>Our research network includes collaborators with ties to Stanford University, Tsinghua University, the University of Wisconsin–Madison, Imperial College London, and frontier AI teams including Qwen. Worldeology operates independently; these affiliations describe research backgrounds and collaborations, not institutional sponsorship.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="lab-page-section about-part" aria-labelledby="focus-title">
      <header><p class="lab-index">02</p><h2 id="focus-title">Research focus.</h2></header>
      <div class="lab-prose">
        <p>We study intelligence as a cognitive trajectory rather than a single answer: how a system understands hidden states, examines its reasoning, learns from experience, and anticipates the consequences of its actions.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="about-focus-list">
        <a class="focus-black" href="/research/cognitive-ai/"><span>Cognitive AI</span><small>Understanding cognition before, during, and after an answer.</small><i>↗</i></a>
        <a class="focus-blue" href="/research/learning-from-cognition/"><span>Learning from Cognition</span><small>Turning cognitive experience into persistent capability.</small><i>↗</i></a>
        <a class="focus-green" href="/research/engine-of-world/"><span>Engine of World</span><small>Modeling persistent worlds and long-horizon consequences.</small><i>↗</i></a>
        <a class="focus-red" href="/research/architecture-of-intelligence/"><span>Architecture of Intelligence</span><small>Redesigning the mechanisms through which models reason.</small><i>↗</i></a>
      </div>
    </section>
    <SiteFooter />
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
